    {
      "path": "/usr/local/var/cyclotron/tmp.noindex/cyclotron-90084b2c/samples/8eba764f2891/github.com-sushitakahashi-review-os-v0.0.0-20260918145704-359826c771f0.zip",
      "sha256": "8eba764f28919bd3c8b490c84063060e835cc8320f34a5db30bb597389cb8c50",
      "identification": "Review-OS repository with concealed Windows Lua payload",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "evidence": [
        "README advertises a local Steam-review web tool and directs users to a ZIP under favicons, including disguising the ZIP URL as image/document/navigation links. The ZIP carries Launcher.cmd, a LuaJIT interpreter/DLL and arch.txt; the batch starts the interpreter with the text file as source.",
        "Recovered decimal-escaped strings, indexed concatenation, a reordered custom radix-64 table and arithmetic-concealed VM state constants. Evaluated only the table-decoder prefix, never the payload. Independently inspected Cleave recovered source and statically partitioned the VM into 546 dispatch leaf intervals.",
        "The recovered Defender branch builds hidden PowerShell Start-Process -Verb runAs with Add-MpPreference -ExclusionPath $env:SystemDrive -ExclusionExtension .exe, .dll -Force and dispatches the command. This is broad security blinding, not ordinary app behavior.",
        "Daily schtasks creation uses randomized times and misleading application-style names; /tn and /tr concatenate a rundll32 DLL invocation. Separate Run-key code opens SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run and calls RegSetValueExW, supporting the added login-persistence detection.",
        "The screenshot implementation obtains screen dimensions, creates compatible/DC and DIB resources and calls BitBlt with SRCCOPY (13369376). WinInet routines initialize connections, form requests and call HttpSendRequestW on a buffer. Manual PE export/PEB resolution, RWX allocations and function-pointer calls are also present and retain existing notable observations.",
        "HTTP/IP, Polygon RPC, host/geolocation and multipart/JSON staging support remote-loader and reporting capabilities. The complete screenshot-to-send chain and final fetched payload were not established, so no new screenshot-exfiltration or final-payload identity claim was added.",
        "Concealed surveillance, broad Defender exclusions, disguised durability and the contradiction with the advertised review web tool establish MALICIOUS without assuming runtime success or deployment permission."
      ],
